      "message": "Sign a person's record the way a receipt is signed\n\nA landing carries a receipt anyone can check without the forge. A\nperson's record now travels the same way: GET\n/api/principals/{id}/record/signed is the figures their page shows,\nfiled under `record` with the forge's Ed25519 signature over the same\ncanonical form, and `ambolt record verify` checks it offline, against\nthe key the document carries or the one you were told to expect. A\nchanged figure fails. The page offers the document in the rail as\n\"Verify this record\".\n\nThe signer learnt to sign any document under a name, and the client to\ncheck any such document, so a receipt and a record are one mechanism\nrather than two.\n\nChange-Id: Irecord0169\nTask: t-7d7rttmrmdaws83rg2rqnc1pc7\nSigned-off-by: Mandip Adhikari <92096340+mandipadk@users.noreply.github.com>",
